c_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.06822338665026739,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":56.1,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.002646436132674665,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":2.6,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.010760577106051472,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":23.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.001184934405416843,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.07582,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":50.5,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Amrize AG engages in the provision of various building solutions for infrastructure, commercial, and residential construction markets in North America and Canada. It operates through two segments, Building Materials and Building Envelope. The Building Materials segment offers cement and aggregates, as well as ready-mix concrete, asphalt, and other construction materials. The Building Envelope segment provides advanced roofing and wall systems, including single-ply membranes, insulation, shingles, sheathing, waterproofing, and protective coatings; and adhesives, tapes, and sealants. The company was formerly known as Holcim North America Finance Ltd and changed its name to Amrize AG in December 2013. Amrize AG was incorporated in 2023 and is based in Zug, Switzerland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jan Philipp Jenisch | CEO & Chairman | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $622K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $75K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $737 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Amrize Ltd is a large-cap basic materials business with a $21.8B market cap on $11.8B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The business throws off $1.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 4.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 7.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (37% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $5.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"15,618 Amrize Ltd $AMRZ Shares Acquired by Narwhal Capital Management","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/15618-amrize-ltd-amrz-shares-acquired-by-narwhal-capital-management.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794394201.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Amrize Ltd (AMRZ) \u2013 What Are Brokerages Thinking About This Stock?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/amrize-ltd-amrz-what-are-brokerages-thinking-about-this-stock.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794388523.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Amrize (NYSE:AMRZ) Stock Bumped Down to Hold by Berenberg Bank","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/amrize-nyseamrz-stock-bumped-down-to-hold-by-berenberg-bank.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794226010.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Amrize (NYSE:AMRZ) Given New $52.00 Price Target at Oppenheimer","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolniano